      "source": [
        "### Bowlers' Wickets Class Legend (Wickets Per Match)\n",
        "\n",
        "*   **Class 1 (WPM < 0.2):** Bowlers taking, on average, less than 0.2 wickets per match.\n",
        "*   **Class 2 (0.2 <= WPM < 0.5):** Bowlers taking, on average, between 0.2 and 0.5 wickets per match.\n",
        "*   **Class 3 (0.5 <= WPM < 1.0):** Bowlers taking, on average, between 0.5 and 1.0 wickets per match.\n",
        "*   **Class 4 (WPM >= 1.0):** Bowlers taking, on average, 1.0 or more wickets per match."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "91090047"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Batter Performance Comparison\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's visualize the top batters based on their average and strike rate. This will highlight our batting benchmarks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 434
        },
        "id": "1580411d",
        "outputId": "7d5ae609-af70-48f8-8ce2-33fb23f7d93c"
      },
      "source": [
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "# Ensure batters_df is sorted for consistent plotting\n",
        "batters_df_sorted_avg = batters_df.sort_values(by='avg_rank', ascending=True)\n",
        "batters_df_sorted_sr = batters_df.sort_values(by='sr_rank', ascending=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create subplots for Average and Strike Rate comparison\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(18, 7))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot Batting Average\n",
        "sns.barplot(\n",
        "    x='average',\n",
        "    y='player',\n",
        "    data=batters_df_sorted_avg,\n",
        "    ax=axes[0],\n",
        "    palette='viridis',\n",
        "    hue='Runs_Class', # Highlight class in the plot\n",
        "    legend=False\n",
        ")\n",
        "axes[0].set_title('Batters by Average (Higher is Better)')\n",
        "axes[0].set_xlabel('Average')\n",
